  "text": {
    "puzzle": "puzzle",
    "card": "Cover eight cells with nonoverlapping domino indicators; remove to backtrack.",
    "domino": "domino tiling board",
    "rectangle": "two-cell coverage and backtracking",
    "hands_empty": "Put down what you hold before changing a placement.",
    "occupied": "That placement is already shown. Remove it individually.",
    "overlap": "Another shown rectangle covers one of these cells. Remove a conflicting choice or choose a different pair.",
    "already_empty": "That placement is already hidden. Choose a shown placement to remove.",
    "coordinates": "The fixed board has two rows A at the far/top edge and B at the near/bottom edge, and columns1 through4 from left to right. Each horizontal h_a1,h_a2,h_a3 or h_b1,h_b2,h_b3 spans the named row and starting column plus the next column. Vertical v_1 through v_4 spans both rows of its named column. Each visible indicator is one whole two-cell rectangle with an attached middle seam.",
    "rules": "Place any of the ten potential rectangles only when it is hidden and no shown rectangle shares either cell. Boundary contact is allowed; interiors cannot overlap. A complete tiling uses four rectangles to cover all eight cells. Remove any shown choice individually; every partial can return to blank. These are ten fixed potential-placement indicators, not four portable conserved dominoes.",
    "solutions": "There are five complete tilings: (h_a1,h_a3,h_b1,h_b3); (h_a3,h_b3,v_1,v_2); (h_a2,h_b2,v_1,v_4); (h_a1,h_b1,v_3,v_4); and (v_1,v_2,v_3,v_4). These action sequences are examples, not an automatic solver.",
    "backtrack": "A genuine dead end shows h_a1,h_a3 and h_b2: the top row is covered, but the two bottom corner cells cannot be paired. Remove only h_b2, then place h_b1 and h_b3 to complete the board. No reset is needed.",
